  "content": {
    "id": "p59-q18-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the tangent to $y=(2x+1)^4$ at the point where $x=-1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$8x+y+7=0$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y(-1)&=(2(-1)+1)^4\\\\y(-1)&=1\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=4(2x+1)^3\\times2\\\\\\frac{dy}{dx}&=8(2x+1)^3\\\\m&=8(2(-1)+1)^3\\\\m&=-8\\end{align*}$$\nThe tangent passes through $(-1,1)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y-y_1&=m(x-x_1)\\\\y-1&=-8(x+1)\\\\y&=-8x-7\\\\8x+y+7&=0\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
